\f1\fs22 While the First Nations Club occupied the top three floors of Derivative Tower, its cigar lounge came as close to the Layer as any Airborne would voluntarily go. Inside, tobacco smoke cloaked its patrons with a kind of Kashmir wool privilege that didn\'92t apologise because it had never been questioned.  \
